## Building this implementation

Run `./compile.sh` from a checkout to create `./executable`. The build uses a
C++17 compiler and the system PCRE2 development library; it does not download
project packages or require the reference executable. All generated files are
excluded by `.gitignore`.

Run the regression suite with:

```sh
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

The implementation is organized into command-line parsing, numeric/time parsing,
regular-expression validation and matching, and the process-execution loop.
Commands are evaluated by `sh`, with `COUNT` and (when iterating values) `ITEM`
provided in the environment. Standard output and standard error are captured
together. Input on a non-terminal standard input is read as a list of items;
`--stdin` forces that behavior on a terminal as well.
